     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Sample space:</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A heart</td>\n<td>A club</td>\n<td>K spade</td>\n<td>10 heart</td>\n<td>9 heart</td>\n<td>9 spade</td>\n<td>9 diamond</td>\n<td>6 club</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The Multiplication Rule for Probability: If <span data-math=\"E\"></span> and <span data-math=\"F\"></span> are events associated with the first and second stages of an experiment, then <span data-math=\"{\\text{P}}\\left( {E\\,{\\text{and}}\\,F} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ P}}\\left( E \\right){\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ P}}\\left( {F|E} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>There are 3 nines to be drawn first out of 8 cards.</p>\n<p>There is 1 six be drawn second out of 7 cards.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{P(a heart, then another heart)  =  }}\\frac{3}{8}\\left( {\\frac{2}{7}} \\right) = \\frac{6}{{56}} = \\frac{3}{{28}}\"></span>.</p>\n"
